## Download and apply the vector

For saved-data publication, use the repository's locked installation and run `uv run --locked --no-sync python scripts/build_ant_publication.py`. Missing evidence is restored from the input manifest's immutable Hub revision `{{source_revision}}`. The builder verifies complete file hashes before rendering and does not load the policy.

The original [vector archive](https://huggingface.co/BurnyCoder/rl-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/1cd00cfcce13bcb86f1c370a71889ce6d34c278e/experiments/ant-classic-005/vectors.npz) and [manifest/selection](https://huggingface.co/BurnyCoder/rl-locomotion-steering-vectors/tree/1cd00cfcce13bcb86f1c370a71889ce6d34c278e/experiments/ant-classic-005) remain pinned. The `lateral` array is already RMS-scaled: its norm is {{norm}}, and strength {{alpha}} applies norm {{offset_norm}}. Load with `numpy.load(path, allow_pickle=False)` without renormalizing. The same archive includes activation controls; `action_biases.npz` is a separate action-space comparator.

The base checkpoint is [Farama-Minari Ant SAC medium](https://huggingface.co/farama-minari/Ant-v5-SAC-medium/tree/{{checkpoint_revision}}), SHA256 `{{checkpoint_sha}}`. It has {{observation_dim}} observation coordinates, {{action_dim}} actions, and {{hidden_dim}} first-layer ReLU units. The intervention begins after {{warmup}} steps. Upstream weights are referenced rather than repackaged. [Video and simulator reproduction](https://github.com/BurnyCoder/reinforcement-learning-locomotion-steering-vectors/blob/main/docs/ant-videos.md) requires the corresponding historical source revision; current source changes must not be hidden by rewriting old cache identities.
